properties.statement:
This is part (a), RECEIPTS, of req:the-mcp-surface-is-sized-for-tokens-per-task, accepted on its own. The broad requirement, parts (b) to (e), stays proposed.

A write replies with:
- the node id;
- which fields changed, with characters before and after;
- every edge the call drew, as a subject-first sentence;
- every warning, and what a shortened field lost (by size, with the prior text available on request, per req:a-revising-write-says-what-it-removed).

It does not reply with the whole stored node, and replace_text does not echo the prior field in full.

Counter-argument kept: replies were made loud on purpose, because a silently dropped paragraph was caught only because the reply showed it. So a receipt keeps every warning and every removal report.

Measured by the two-agent exercise (I4): a 12-character append returned 7,501 characters, and about 290 KB was echoed for about 40 KB of edits over three rounds.
